@startuml owner-view-gate-protocol
' ============================================================================
' One owner operation of the view-gate model, with close and reopen (leaf G01
' of task 7931). Every action is an action of ViewSpec in
' formal/tlaplus/stack_safe_pda/RSpaceJournalPublicationOwner.tla, whose
' configuration is RSpaceJournalPublicationOwnerViews.cfg.
'   BLUE   #BBDEFB  the caller's locks: the view gate first, the owner mutex
'                   second
'   AMBER  #FFE0B2  a publication that is still pending: reconciliation and
'                   the outcomes that leave the record open
'   PURPLE #E1BEE7  the decisions of the operation
'   RED    #FFCDD2  the three refusals, before anything is captured
'   GREEN  #C8E6C9  the effects of an admitted operation: capture, publish,
'                   acknowledge, activate
'   GREY   #CFD8DC  the return, which releases the call's locks
'   TEAL   #B2DFDB  close and reopen, only while the owner is quiescent
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #E1BEE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #455A64

title <b>One owner operation of the view-gate model, with close and reopen</b>\nThe caller takes its gate first and the owner mutex second, and the owner checks before it captures

start
partition "the caller's locks" {
  :CallCheckpoint, CallReset or CallSpawn: the caller takes a gate
  before it calls the owner. A checkpoint takes its permit's gate,
  a reset its own gate, a spawn both gates with both callers idle.;<<#BBDEFB>>
  :TakeMutex: the view now holds the owner mutex.
  Holding it, the owner never waits for a gate (LockOrder).;<<#BBDEFB>>
}
partition "reconcile first" {
  while (a publication is pending?) is (yes)
    :ReconcileFirst: the holder can only resolve the record,
    even one captured through the other view's gate.;<<#FFE0B2>>
    note right #FFF3E0
      <b>Resolve</b>
      RecoveryRequired, root unchanged: the predecessor stands,
      the record's gate is freed and the record is cleared.
      RecoveryRequired, root moved: the record enters AwaitingAck.
      AwaitingAck: the view's base becomes the root unless it was
      already acknowledged, the gate is freed, the record is cleared.
      With the mutex free, ReconcilePending applies the same Resolve.
    end note
  endwhile (no)
}
partition "CheckRequest decides before anything is captured, then the admitted operation runs" {
  if (a checkpoint whose permit is another view's gate?) then (yes)
    :result "refused-permit";<<#FFCDD2>>
  else (no)
    if (the attachment's incarnation differs from the owner's?) then (yes)
      :result "refused-incarnation";<<#FFCDD2>>
    else (no)
      if (a checkpoint whose base is not the owner's root?) then (yes)
        :result "refused-base";<<#FFCDD2>>
      else (no)
        if (which operation?) then (checkpoint)
          :capture: the pending record takes the view, the permit
          and the base, in phase Captured, and the permit's gate
          is marked pending, so the return does not free it.;<<#C8E6C9>>
          switch (PublishView: the outcome of the publication?)
          case (new)
            :the root moves and the record
            enters AwaitingAck.;<<#C8E6C9>>
            :AcknowledgeView: the view's base
            becomes the new root.;<<#C8E6C9>>
            if (the acknowledgement completes?) then (yes)
              :the gate is freed, the record is
              cleared, result "acknowledged";<<#C8E6C9>>
            else (no)
              :the record keeps one acknowledgement,
              the gate stays pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
            endif
          case (unknown-new)
            :the root moves, the record enters
            RecoveryRequired, the gate stays
            pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
          case (unknown-old)
            :the root is kept, the record enters
            RecoveryRequired, the gate stays
            pending, result "uncertain";<<#FFE0B2>>
          endswitch
        else (reset or spawn)
          :ApplyActivation: a reset moves the root to its
          target and reattaches the view there, result "reset".
          A spawn moves the root to the source view's base and
          attaches the other view to the same owner at that
          base, result "spawned".;<<#C8E6C9>>
        endif
      endif
    endif
  endif
}
:ReturnCall: the mutex and every gate that this call holds are freed.
A gate marked pending stays held by its record.;<<#CFD8DC>>
stop

start
partition "close and reopen" {
  :CloseOwner, only on a live, quiescent owner within its session bound:
  live becomes false and the incarnation is retired, so every
  attachment taken before the close fails the incarnation check.;<<#B2DFDB>>
  :ReopenOwner, only on a closed, quiescent owner: live becomes true,
  FreshIncarnation installs a new incarnation, the session
  advances, and one view attaches at the current root.;<<#B2DFDB>>
  note right #E0F2F1
    A view that kept its old attachment is
    refused with "refused-incarnation".
  end note
}
stop

legend right
  <b>Legend</b>
  <back:#BBDEFB> blue </back> the caller's locks
  <back:#FFE0B2> amber </back> a publication still pending
  <back:#E1BEE7> purple </back> a decision of the operation
  <back:#FFCDD2> red </back> a refusal before any capture
  <back:#C8E6C9> green </back> the effects of an admitted operation
  <back:#CFD8DC> grey </back> the return
  <back:#B2DFDB> teal </back> close and reopen
endlegend
@enduml
